+### Null-texture specialization
+
+`air.is_null_texture` of a `[[texture(n)]]` argument asks whether the consumer bound anything at
+Metal slot `n`, which only the consumer knows. Translation therefore lowers that query to a
+specialization constant: an `OpSpecConstantFalse` decorated `SpecId NULL_TEXTURE_SPEC_ID_BASE + n`.
+Unspecialized, the module behaves as if every declared texture were bound. When the consumer
+creates a pipeline for a draw that leaves slot `n` unbound (and substitutes a placeholder
+descriptor so the layout stays complete), it sets that constant to `VK_TRUE` through
+`VkSpecializationInfo`; the shader then takes the branch it takes on Metal for an unbound
+argument instead of sampling the placeholder. A constant id the module does not declare is
+ignored, so a consumer may name every unbound slot without asking which ones the shader tests.
+Only a texture loaded straight from its argument has such a constant; `is_null_texture` of a
+texture reached through an argument buffer or a descriptor array stays the constant false, and of
+a value from `air.get_null_texture_*` stays the constant true.
+
 ## Typical consumer flow
 
 1. Call `translate_reflected` (or a serde-enabled CLI with `--emit-meta`).
