+/// Vulkan specialization-constant ids answering `air.is_null_texture` for a declared texture
+/// argument: the constant for `[[texture(n)]]` has id `NULL_TEXTURE_SPEC_ID_BASE + n` and is
+/// emitted as `OpSpecConstantFalse`, so an unspecialized module behaves as if every declared
+/// texture were bound. A consumer that leaves a declared texture argument unbound sets that id to
+/// `VK_TRUE` when it creates the pipeline, which is the answer the shader gets on Metal for an
+/// argument nothing was bound to. Only a texture loaded straight from its argument has such a
+/// constant; an argument-buffer or array texture keeps the constant false. Ids below the base are
+/// the dispatch-region ids; the range above it spans [`TEXTURE_ARGUMENT_COUNT`] indices.
+pub const NULL_TEXTURE_SPEC_ID_BASE: u32 = 16;
+
